{"agent_id":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","agent_seq":52,"timestamp":"2026-08-29T03:56:39.634924691Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1dfdeb3-a85a-402c-b912-8b26718693f5","comment_uuid":"3951258e-657c-47d3-98bf-a976b3df9eb3","author":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","content":"Result: Shell startup alias delivered — 'opencode' now defaults to the KEEPER worktree on login (issue #510, recurring task; prior kickoffs pp3g-DgXe / pp3g-XAmt failed at the sandbox gate that blocked writes to the operator shell startup — sandbox now fixed, so the write succeeded).\n\nWHAT: Created ~/.bash_aliases (sourced by ~/.bashrc, which ~/.profile sources on login) exporting ASES_KEEPER_WT=/home/claude-code/projects/ASES/.worktrees/stop-button (commit 90458364), a 'keeper' function (cd to the keeper wt), and an 'opencode' function that launches the real ~/.local/bin/opencode launcher inside the keeper worktree by default. Smart-default: keeper when cwd is not already a git project (so other worktrees still work); respects current project when you are inside one. The claude wrapper calls the launcher by absolute path, so it is unaffected.\n\nWHY: The operator wants, on login, opencode to open the surviving 'keeper' worktree (feature/stop-button) by default rather than requiring a manual cd. This is an environment convenience, not a code change, so it lives in the operator home, not the repo.\n\nHOW CERTAIN: Evidence-based. Verified: bash -n syntax OK; both keeper and opencode resolve as functions after source; keeper cds to the keeper wt; smart-default condition selects keeper from /home/claude-code and PWD inside a git repo; end-to-end 'opencode --version' from /home/claude-code cd's into the keeper and the launcher fork-identity guard passes (prints 1.18.13-pp3g-fork). Sourcing chain ~/.profile -> ~/.bashrc -> ~/.bash_aliases confirmed.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: Did not launch the interactive opencode TUI (would block); verified the launcher chain via --version instead. Did not test an actual SSH/login shell spawn, but the sourcing chain is standard and verified. Pre-existing unrelated working-tree changes were left untouched: .opencode/agents/reviewer.md (mode primary->subagent) and untracked .crosslink/sandbox/restrict.sh — these are out of scope for this alias task and were not committed.","created_at":"2026-08-29T03:56:39.628573124Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAMFeZ0JaCbsz6TWkppCOoOo6iwXQaQYazzqNIOSCVtuWFHHIfS3elijV1JBl9lKm6PVet2nZUsH8WkZXlfiElDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIXxNwO+VGzjxqbZWqdgvUHcJJ/7F5m9aKK+iVgFg7e/rJa/ny2NPFpu028qGCz/4Ns/8CSYiWjOfXVe5ieZBg0="}
