{"agent_id":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","agent_seq":65,"timestamp":"2026-08-29T04:24:38.556329665Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1dfdeb3-a85a-402c-b912-8b26718693f5","comment_uuid":"e245e464-9864-4444-8dd5-ad38b215ef0b","author":"pp3g-LB3f-stop-button-phase-0-6-point-interrupt-probe-then-tiny","content":"Result: Fixed the opencode2 shell alias (crosslink #510) to run the KEEPER FORK DEV SERVER instead of the official @opencode-ai/cli binary.\n\nWHAT: ~/.bash_aliases opencode2() previously invoked 'command opencode2' (official binary, v0.0.0-beta-17963). It now cds into the keeper fork source ($ASES_KEEPER_WT/fork/opencode-src, node_modules already installed) and runs 'bun run dev', launching the dev build of the pp3g fork TUI with hot reload. The project it opens defaults to the keeper worktree, or the current git project when cwd is already inside one (smart-default preserved from the prior opencode2); user-supplied args/flags pass through unchanged (e.g. 'opencode2 /some/dir', 'opencode2 --model x'). Added guards: clear error + exit 1 if the fork source dir is missing or 'bun' is not on PATH. Header comment updated to state opencode2 runs the fork dev server (and the 'force keeper' snippet no longer references command opencode2).\n\nWHY: The operator wants opencode2 to open a dev instance of the fork (the keeper worktree's fork source) rather than the published official binary — so fork changes are exercisable live with hot reload.\n\nHOW CERTAIN: Evidence-based. Verified: bash -n syntax OK; 'type opencode2' resolves as a function; 'bun run dev --version' boots the fork entry and prints 'local' (the source/dev build version, NOT the official binary's v0.0.0-beta-17963) — proving node_modules resolve and arg forwarding works; 'bun run dev /abs/path --help' parses a project path positional without error (proves the keeper/current-project path reaches the TUI as its [project] argument); sentinel test with a missing fork source returns exit 1 with a clear message; smart-default probe confirms keeper from $HOME and /tmp, current project from inside a git repo.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: Did not launch the interactive TUI (would block); verified the launch chain via --version/--help instead. Did not test an actual login shell spawn, but the sourcing chain (~/.profile -> ~/.bashrc -> ~/.bash_aliases) is standard and unchanged. Deliverable lives in operator home (~/.bash_aliases), not the repo, so no git commit is required for this change. Pre-existing unrelated working-tree changes (reviewer.md mode, sandbox/restrict.sh) left untouched.","created_at":"2026-08-29T04:24:38.550125628Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA+249feqqoa26nIi9nTHwvagjAYliJ1RdIroU4Y3HzKyQQU3RLtlk9L/kWnDpmliOSv8kK5XgPxopg4xdGdqeDw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:LKcxcY8ErII3ow2tdjEolL0oRExAkZLj6VIU4Cf0vsU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg2i4aIKoWd/MjdlgxwIzpP8HLAqXTaHiEwqkQ2J/7hTUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDOHt56Mmzezrqavr5evHFXZoSRRJXSov3i3kdSiRrzgxo4JQHymdAoDDhSXYSELOkcD5zVwGMx4aQv6ftBMvAM="}
